The reviewers’ comments are mixed. They raise concerns regarding:
(1) the novelty over the work of Than and Phan https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.07325---the paper under review builds on top of the framework established by Than and Phan;
(2) the requirement of bounded loss function;
(3) how the data space Z is partitioned so that the upper bound is tight and robust;
(4) the complexity of the upper bound and its dependence on the data space partition---the upper bound is not neat enough, to say the least;
(5) the possibility of a mistake in the proof of theorem B.5; and
(6) the scope of empirical evaluation.
